  "reproduction": [
    "Restore m3-draw-start.ppst paused; run prepare_duel_boundary with last-draw/empty-draw, player 1, expected 35. Capture before. Resume original code to Standby for last draw, or duel-end display for empty draw. Restore and repeat.",
    "Restore m3-attack-baseline.ppst paused; prepare low-lp, player 1, expected 8000. Confirm Attack with Circle; decline optional activation with Right, Circle. Resume through canonical LP store and win display. Restore and repeat.",
    "Natural battle: turn-one Krebons, turn-three Tin Goldfish in attack position, decline effects, end turn. Opponent summons Chick and resolves Graceful Dice. Replay the retained damage-store anchor (Dice rolled 2) twice; watch zone 3 destruction and step original instructions until Tin reaches its graveyard."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Deck and lethal-LP inputs use one canonical RAM-field write per setup. They were not reached naturally. Inactive deck-tail entries and presentation mirrors remain unchanged.",
    "The lethal run UI LP number animates from the unmodified presentation mirror (8000 to 6800); only canonical LP and the explicit original-game win message support defeat.",
    "Monster battle starts at the original damage-store instruction after the game calculated damage. It validates the retained combat input and resulting damage/destruction, not attack declaration or response windows.",
    "Early watch-tool transcripts omit raw resume/step requests; CPU before/after records, watch reports and RAM snapshots retain the observations. The current helper logs those requests.",
    "The combat C# test substitutes already observed current stats; it does not reproduce Graceful Dice, its RNG, Monster Reborn, effect resolution or AI.",
    "C# draw/LP tests reach their boundaries through legal synthetic command sequences; native turn numbers, hand/deck contents and unrelated cards are excluded from those comparisons.",
    "Raw outcome fields are retained as measurements for these two wins, not a universal decoded result enum. No native bytes are matched."
  ]
